WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.740
To those politicians supported by the NRA

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:06.220
that allow the continued slaughter of our
children and our future

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.220
I say 'get your resumes ready.'

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.040
The students of Stoneman Douglas High School
in Parkland, Florida

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.480
have reenergized the national movement to
restrict gun ownership

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.360
following the tragic mass shooting that claimed
17 lives.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:25.180
The culmination of this movement was the massive
March for Our Lives Rally in Washington, D.C.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.420
I'm here to help stop gun violence.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.900
I just think enough is enough and I don't
want to see any more lives being lost.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.120
I want less children to die.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.120
We can and we will change the world.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.320
The students from Stoneman Douglas have earned
praise for their leadership

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.480
in demanding that Congress take decisive action.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.160
But there’s another consequence of this
movement,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.080
which is that the Parkland mass shooting

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.249
seems to be stoking irrational fear about
gun violence in schools.

00:00:51.249 --> 00:00:53.220
I'm here 'cause I want to feel safe in my
school.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.340
You’d come away from the March for Our Lives

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.560
thinking that there’s a mass shooting epidemic
in American schools.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.159
I do think that it's more dangerous in schools.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.220
There's more school shootings now.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.620
We're all in danger.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.540
But what happened at Stoneman Douglas was
an extremely rare occurrence.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.640
American schools are profoundly safe, and
most likely getting safer:

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.820
According to researchers at Northeastern University,

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.040
shooting incidents involving students have
actually decreased in recent years,

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.520
and in the 1990s the overall crime rate was
much higher than it is today.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.160
The rate of homicides from firearms in the
U.S. has plummeted.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:31.280
In fact, students are orders of magnitude
more likely to die in a car crash

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.820
on their way to school

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.780
than they are to be gunned down in their classrooms.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:40.200
Yet the protesters were demanding more security
in schools—a lot more

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.780
So do you think there should be more police
officers in schools?

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.980
Yeah, definitely.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:48.620
Trained officers or security guards should
be the ones protecting students.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:52.600
—even if it means making armed guards a
fixture of the lives of children.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.400
I support sensible gun policy.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.380
It's simple, no guns, less violence.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.560
We should stop having guns anywhere at all

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.360
like I feel like guns should be outlawed.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.580
I would just like to see guns illegal.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:06.500
This latest hysteria over mass shootings and
guns

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.240
is leading to claims that we must relinquish
our rights in the name of safety,

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.980
which is a familiar story, from the drug war
to the war on terror.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.440
Teenagers have every right to fight for a
cause they believe in,

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.650
and the students from Stoneman Douglas are
justifiably enraged

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:24.310
about an event that claimed the lives of so
many friends and classmates.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.460
But feelings shouldn’t trump facts

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:30.800
and we should never craft policies from a
place of fear in the wake of tragedy.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.800
There should be more regulations, or there
should just be more laws

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.400
there just needs to be something happening,
thoughts and prayers don't do much anymore.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.720
It's just, I'm just getting tired of it.

